 "intro": "Moving the object to the front, the pronoun that must then repeat it, things that happen by themselves, and le for lo.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "duplicar",
   "significado": "to double, to repeat",
   "pron": "du-pli-KAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In grammar, to «duplicar» the object is to repeat it with a pronoun: «a Juan lo vi».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "énfasis",
   "significado": "emphasis",
   "pron": "EN-fa-sis",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent: EN-fa-sis. It is masculine: «el énfasis». It does not change in the plural.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "destacar",
   "significado": "to highlight",
   "pron": "des-ta-KAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Moving the object forward highlights it: «el libro lo compré ayer». The c sounds k.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "leísmo",
   "significado": "use of le instead of lo",
   "pron": "le-IS-mo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The RAE accepts it only for a male person: «le vi». Not for things: «lo compré».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "romperse",
   "significado": "to break (by itself)",
   "pron": "rrom-PER-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With «se» there is nobody to blame: «se rompió el vaso». With «me»: «se me rompió».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "estropearse",
   "significado": "to break down",
   "pron": "es-tro-pe-AR-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A machine or a car breaks down: «se me estropeó el paraguas».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "apagarse",
   "significado": "to go out, to switch off",
   "pron": "a-pa-GAR-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A light «se apaga» by itself. If you do it, «apago la luz». The g is hard: a-pa-GAR-se.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "caerse",
   "significado": "to fall, to drop",
   "pron": "ka-ER-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is irregular: «se me cayó». It has two vowels together: ka-ER-se.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "perderse",
   "significado": "to get lost",
   "pron": "per-DER-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With «se me» it is something that vanishes with nobody to blame: «se me perdieron las llaves».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "mancharse",
   "significado": "to get stained",
   "pron": "man-CHAR-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Something gets stained by itself or by accident: «se me manchó la camisa». The ch sounds as in «chocolate».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "sin querer",
   "significado": "by accident",
   "pron": "sin ke-RER",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is used to say it was not intended: «lo rompí sin querer».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "a propósito",
   "significado": "on purpose; by the way",
   "pron": "a pro-PO-si-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is the opposite of «sin querer»: «lo hice a propósito». It also serves to change the subject.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "habrán",
